<title>GERMANY: DTB sets new margin parameters effective Feb 13.</title>
<headline>DTB sets new margin parameters effective Feb 13.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's electronic futures exchange on Wednesday set the following margin parameters for several instruments. The conditions will become efffective on Thursday, February 13.</p>
<p>    MARGIN CLASS  PRODUCTS IN CLASS   PRVS    NEW PARAMETERS</p>
<p>    BUND	    Bund		    1.6 pts     1.5 pts</p>
<p>			OBND		    (4,000 dmk) (3,750 dmk)</p>
<p>			spread rates	  300 dmk     300 dmk</p>
<p>						  back month  back month</p>
<p>						  650 dmk     650 dmk</p>
<p>						  spot month  spot month</p>
<p>    BOBL	    Bobl		    1.4 pts     1.2 pts</p>
<p>			OBOB		    (3,500 dmk) (3,000 dmk)</p>
<p>			spread		  400 dmk     400 dmk</p>
<p>						  back month  back month</p>
<p>						  600 dmk     600 dmk</p>
<p>						  spot month  spot month</p>
<p>    MDAX	    FMDX		    120 pts     100 pts</p>
<p>						  (1,200 dmk) (1,000 dmk)</p>
<p>						  80 dmk	80 dmk</p>
<p>						  back month  back month</p>
<p>						  80 dmk	80 dmk</p>
<p>						  spot month  spot month</p>
<p>    USD					 6 pct	 3 pct</p>
<p>	  --Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
